# Beat The Hazard - environment configuration example
# Copy to .env and fill in what you want. NEVER commit the real .env file.
#
# Every one of these is optional. With none of them set the game still works
# fully: sign in with a name, or with a passkey, and optionally add an
# authenticator app. Only the social buttons need configuring.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in  —  works with no backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services -> Credentials
# 2. Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application
# 3. Under "Authorised JavaScript origins" add BOTH:
#       http://localhost:5173
#       https://kushalthewave.github.io
# 4. Paste the Client ID below. There is no secret for this flow.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Facebook sign-in  —  works with no backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# developers.facebook.com -> Create App -> add "Facebook Login" -> Settings.
# Add this site under "Valid OAuth Redirect URIs". Only the App ID is needed.
VITE_FACEBOOK_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub sign-in  —  REQUIRES A SMALL BACKEND
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub's token exchange needs the client SECRET and its endpoint sends no
# CORS headers, so a browser cannot complete the flow. Putting a secret in
# front-end code would publish it to everyone.
#
# To enable it, deploy a one-function endpoint (Cloudflare Workers, Netlify
# Functions and Vercel all have free tiers) that accepts { code } and returns
# the GitHub user profile, keeping the secret server-side.
#
# Until VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENDPOINT is set, the GitHub button stays disabled and
# explains why rather than failing silently.
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional analytics / backend endpoint (unused by the offline core game)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
